model {
  extend basalt.poolRuntime {
    metadata {
      constraint "The resumable-stream front layer listens on its own port and receives only finite model calls the controller marks resumable and resume reads. Model sockets, unmarked calls, the model lifetime socket and node health stay on the node's port untouched. The layer forwards request and answer bytes unchanged, opens one node connection per call and closes it when the upstream ends, so the legacy drain counts each call through the layer exactly once and never an idle connection. A marked call with a fresh canonical request id and a successful answer is buffered as raw bytes; any other call passes through unbuffered. The buffered upstream runs on its own context and keeps being read after its reader leaves. Bytes not yet written to a reader are never dropped: reading pauses while the unsent backlog fills the retain window, and the kept window is the most recent bytes behind the write position. The write position counts bytes handed to the reader's connection, including any written before the layer notices it closed. The layer counts a write once that write returns, so a resume from the client's own read position is answered from the layer once the layer has counted the write, and in the moment before that it can be answered gone. The resume tests wait until the layer has seen the reader go before they resume. All buffers draw fixed-size chunks from one counted pool with a hard limit; at the limit only written bytes are freed, from finished calls first, and no call with a reader is cancelled. A buffer without a reader for the idle limit is dropped and its upstream cancelled. A resume read names the boot, attaches as the only reader, replaces an older one, and answers gone for an unknown id, a dropped buffer, an offset outside the window, another boot or a failed upstream. An upstream that fails mid-answer aborts the reader's connection instead of ending it. The supervisor runs the layer outside the Home and node generation: its exit never ends the container, it restarts alone with backoff, and readiness names resume only while the layer answers its own health check. An image without the layer never names resume."
    }
  }
}
